  "worked_solution": "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =11+5 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=CH=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{2} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
